---
import StaticPageLayout from "../layouts/StaticPageLayout.astro";
---

<StaticPageLayout
  title="Frequently Asked Questions"
  seoTitle="TipPal — Frequently Asked Questions"
  description="Answers to common questions about TipPal: the app, your account, identity verification (KYC), payments and withdrawals, security and privacy, and getting started."
  lastUpdated="August 10, 2026"
  canonicalURL="/faq"
  hreflang={{ en: "/faq", es: "/es/faq" }}
>
  <section>
    <p>Quick answers to the questions we hear most. If you can't find what you need, <a href="/contact">contact us</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ General ═══ -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="legal__part-title">General</h2>

    <details id="general-what-is-tippal">
      <summary>What is TipPal?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>TipPal is the first app built exclusively for expressing gratitude in person. You can send a gift or a thank-you to anyone who made your day — rideshare drivers, restaurant staff, hotel housekeeping, valets, content creators, and more — using Tap to Pay on your phone, without pressure and without cash.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="general-where-available">
      <summary>Where is TipPal available?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>TipPal currently operates in the United States and launched in Orlando, Florida. We are planning to expand to more regions over time. Availability may depend on local regulations and our payment processor's coverage.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="general-need-account">
      <summary>Do I need an account to use TipPal?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>Yes. You need a TipPal account to send or receive gratitude and to withdraw your balance. Creating an account requires an email address and the personal information needed to verify your identity.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="general-is-tippal-a-bank">
      <summary>Is TipPal a bank?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>No. TipPal is not a bank, is not an independently authorized money transmitter, and does not offer FDIC-insured deposit accounts. TipPal is a technology platform that facilitates payment processing between users through our payment processor, Stripe, Inc.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ Account & KYC ═══ -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="legal__part-title">Account &amp; KYC</h2>

    <details id="kyc-what-is">
      <summary>What is KYC and why is it required?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>KYC stands for "Know Your Customer" — the identity verification process required by U.S. anti-money laundering laws, including the Bank Secrecy Act. We complete KYC to confirm you are who you say you are and to help prevent fraud and illicit activity.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="kyc-when-required">
      <summary>When do I need to complete identity verification?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>You can create an account and start receiving gratitude right away. You will need to complete KYC before you can cash out (withdraw funds to an external bank account or card). We may also ask for verification at other points to comply with regulatory requirements.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="account-who-can-create">
      <summary>Who can create a TipPal account?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>You must be at least 18 years old, have the legal capacity to enter into an agreement in your jurisdiction, and use the Service in compliance with all applicable U.S. federal, state, and local laws.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="account-how-to-delete">
      <summary>How do I delete my account?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>You can request account deletion at any time by emailing <a href="mailto:support@tippalcorp.com">support@tippalcorp.com</a> from the email registered to your account. See our <a href="/delete-account">account deletion page</a> for step-by-step instructions and what data is removed.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ Payments & Withdrawals ═══ -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="legal__part-title">Payments &amp; Withdrawals</h2>

    <details id="payments-how-send">
      <summary>How do I send gratitude?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>Open the TipPal app, choose the person you want to thank, enter the amount you'd like to give, and hold your phone near theirs (or use Tap to Pay) to complete the gesture. You can also send gratitude to registered TipPal users directly in the app.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="payments-how-withdraw">
      <summary>How do I cash out my balance?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>To withdraw your balance (cash out), you must first complete identity verification (KYC). Once verified, you can transfer available funds to an external bank account or card. Withdrawals may be delayed, suspended, or rejected if verification is incomplete or during compliance reviews.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="payments-what-is-balance">
      <summary>What is the balance shown in the app?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>The balance displayed in the app is an accounting record of credit in your favor — a pending settlement, not a bank deposit, a securities account, or an insured financial product. It does not earn interest. See our <a href="/legal#terms">Terms of Service</a> for the full description.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="payments-transfer-to-user">
      <summary>Can I send my balance to another TipPal user?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>Yes. Registered users can transfer their available balance to other TipPal users within the app. These internal transfers are accounting adjustments, not new external financial transactions, and do not require KYC unless one party withdraws to an external bank account or card.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="payments-funds-insured">
      <summary>Are my funds FDIC-insured?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>No. TipPal is not a bank and does not offer FDIC-insured deposit accounts. The balance shown is not a bank deposit. Funds are processed and held through our payment processor, Stripe, under TipPal's processing credentials until verification requirements are completed.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ Security & Privacy ═══ -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="legal__part-title">Security &amp; Privacy</h2>

    <details id="security-who-processes">
      <summary>Who processes my payments?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>Payments are processed by Stripe, Inc., a registered payment processor. TipPal operates as a technology platform (Payment Facilitator) and facilitates the processing of charges on your behalf through Stripe. See our <a href="/security">security page</a> for more detail.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="security-data-protected">
      <summary>How is my personal data protected?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>TipPal implements reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect your information, including encryption in transit and at rest where applicable. No system is completely secure, but we follow industry practices to safeguard your data. Details are in our <a href="/legal#privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="security-who-sees-data">
      <summary>Who can see my personal information?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>We share your information only with the service providers necessary to operate TipPal — including Stripe (payment processing), Resend (email), Google Firebase (infrastructure and notifications), and our hosting providers — plus business partners as needed, and authorities when required by law. See <a href="/legal#privacy">Privacy Policy Section 5</a> for the complete list.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="security-privacy-rights">
      <summary>How do I exercise my privacy rights?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>You can request access to, correction of, or deletion of your personal data, subject to legal record-keeping obligations. Email our data-protection channel at <a href="mailto:info@tippalcorp.com">info@tippalcorp.com</a>, or see <a href="/legal#privacy">Privacy Policy Section 6</a> for your rights.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══ Getting the App ═══ -->
  <section>
    <h2 class="legal__part-title">Getting the App</h2>

    <details id="get-where-download">
      <summary>Where can I download TipPal?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>TipPal is available on the App Store for iPhone and on Google Play for Android devices. Visit the TipPal home page for direct download links.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="get-app-free">
      <summary>Is the TipPal app free to download?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>Yes, the TipPal app is free to download from the App Store and Google Play. Any charges that may apply to specific transactions, withdrawals, or premium features are always disclosed to you before you complete an action. See our <a href="/legal#terms">Terms of Service</a> for the full terms.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="get-contact-support">
      <summary>How do I contact support?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>For help with your account, payments, or the app, email <a href="mailto:support@tippalcorp.com">support@tippalcorp.com</a>. For privacy-related questions, email <a href="mailto:info@tippalcorp.com">info@tippalcorp.com</a>. See our <a href="/contact">contact page</a> for more ways to reach us.</p>
      </div>
    </details>

    <details id="get-lost-access">
      <summary>What if I lose access to my account?</summary>
      <div class="faq__answer">
        <p>If you can't sign in or you lost access to the email registered to your account, contact <a href="mailto:support@tippalcorp.com">support@tippalcorp.com</a> right away and include your TipPal username or TipPal ID so we can verify your identity and help you recover access.</p>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
</StaticPageLayout>